(5451942, 781551, 69504, '<td valign="top">This is one of my favorites. I am big fan of your photography and perspective. Like the way you use your kitchen for photography, probably no one ever might have thought that kitchen could serve a purpose other than cooking. Congratulations! again on the ribbon.</td>', 'This is one of my favorites. I am big fan of your photography and perspective. Like the way you use your kitchen for photography, probably no one ever might have thought that kitchen could serve a purpose other than cooking. Congratulations! again on the ribbon.', '2009-04-25 14:35:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(5452269, 780931, 66515, '<td valign="top">I really like the idea. Hard to execute unfortunately. The shadows are harsh and its hard to actually see the colors  (the purple and the green are quite dark). The other colors also look a bit oversaturated. <br/> <br/>One thing that might have worked (whether it would be an improvement or not may be debatable) is to actually color the page rather than having melted wax. <br/> <br/>In the end, this was a really great idea that was pretty tough to pull off.</td>', 'I really like the idea. Hard to execute unfortunately. The shadows are harsh and its hard to actually see the colors  (the purple and the green are quite dark). The other colors also look a bit oversaturated.  One thing that might have worked (whether it would be an improvement or not may be debatable) is to actually color the page rather than having melted wax.  In the end, this was a really great idea that was pretty tough to pull off.', '2009-04-25 23:44:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5452336, 781797, 92512, '<td valign="top">Critique club comment by rodfulk<br/> <br/>Good idea and well done!<br/>The blunt pencils being subject is well in focus, while the work is lightly blurred.<br/>The angle of pencils and draker colored background draws you to negitive space between to two,at the bluntpoint of the pencils.</td>', 'Critique club comment by rodfulk Good idea and well done!The blunt pencils being subject is well in focus, while the work is lightly blurred.The angle of pencils and draker colored background draws you to negitive space between to two,at the bluntpoint of the pencils.', '2009-04-26 00:49:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(5452345, 781794, 92512, '<td valign="top">Critique club comment by rodfulk;<br/> <br/>Your Dof works but seems to have a little motion blur as well.<br/>Which is okay if your going foe a wave effect. Hince the title. But the blur should been horizonal insteed of vetical. IMO.<br/>The OOF pencil in front is a little distracting as well.<br/>I like the idea, one could the pencil ppoints looks like waves in the sea.</td>', 'Critique club comment by rodfulk; Your Dof works but seems to have a little motion blur as well.Which is okay if your going foe a wave effect. Hince the title. But the blur should been horizonal insteed of vetical. IMO.The OOF pencil in front is a little distracting as well.I like the idea, one could the pencil ppoints looks like waves in the sea.', '2009-04-26 00:58:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(5452352, 781753, 92512, '<td valign="top">Critiques from the club via rodfulk;<br/> <br/>Very unique and creative. The post processing was well done and very artistic.<br/>Good work on the eye. Good you captured the texture of the face and did not lose it in processing.<br/>I also think that the frame helped out quite a bit here hold the attention of the veiwer towrds the center. Where as without it, ones eyes would run up the arm and off the picture.</td>', 'Critiques from the club via rodfulk; Very unique and creative. The post processing was well done and very artistic.Good work on the eye. Good you captured the texture of the face and did not lose it in processing.I also think that the frame helped out quite a bit here hold the attention of the veiwer towrds the center. Where as without it, ones eyes would run up the arm and off the picture.', '2009-04-26 01:09:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(5452454, 781783, 66515, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club!<br/> <br/>Interesting idea for this challenge. Not sure how the water droplets were intended to enhance the picture. (Not saying that they don''t its just that <i><b>I</b></i> don''t see it..) <br/> <br/>Good lighting and exposure for this shot. Focus is bang on as well. Composition is interesting but it seems like there''s something missing. Perhaps if they were all lined up evently or perhaps in an interesting arrangement. (e.g. created a diaganol line or a wave perhaps?)<br/> <br/>Overall a pretty decent shot.</td>', 'Greetings from the critique club! Interesting idea for this challenge. Not sure how the water droplets were intended to enhance the picture. (Not saying that they don''t its just that I don''t see it..)  Good lighting and exposure for this shot. Focus is bang on as well. Composition is interesting but it seems like there''s something missing. Perhaps if they were all lined up evently or perhaps in an interesting arrangement. (e.g. created a diaganol line or a wave perhaps?) Overall a pretty decent shot.', '2009-04-26 03:35:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(5453037, 781673, 73942, '<td valign="top">Chris, creative entry with a nice finish, congrats!</td>', 'Chris, creative entry with a nice finish, congrats!', '2009-04-26 22:22:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(5453276, 781549, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: Basically a good colourful shot of a popular theme in this challenge, but lacking in the WOW factor.  In voting I would have given this a 6.<br/> <br/>Technical: Good even lighting, but a bit flat.  The pov is fine for this sort of immediate overhead shot; the dof could use a little work as it does look a little soft.   Good use of thirds and lines.  <br/> <br/>Artistic: I love that the ends of the pencils have that odd white band, it really helps draw attention to the heart...<br/> <br/>FWIW: ...in fact, I would have cropped this way down to drive home the shape, and really hit it with the saturation, then after resizing, used unsharp mask at least once and probably sharpen edges too.<br/> <br/>Overall a pleasant pic and very well done in terms of execution, just needs a little more tweaking to make it pop.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions.<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: Basically a good colourful shot of a popular theme in this challenge, but lacking in the WOW factor.  In voting I would have given this a 6. Technical: Good even lighting, but a bit flat.  The pov is fine for this sort of immediate overhead shot; the dof could use a little work as it does look a little soft.   Good use of thirds and lines.   Artistic: I love that the ends of the pencils have that odd white band, it really helps draw attention to the heart... FWIW: ...in fact, I would have cropped this way down to drive home the shape, and really hit it with the saturation, then after resizing, used unsharp mask at least once and probably sharpen edges too. Overall a pleasant pic and very well done in terms of execution, just needs a little more tweaking to make it pop. Feel free to PM me with any questions. Susan', '2009-04-27 00:55:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(5455202, 779890, 99993, '<td valign="top">Thank you snaffles. You have given me plenty of food for thought. I really like IreneMs work and sure would like to try a similar shot some time. I need a remote flash! As for this shot I am happy with the score. I realised it lacked sharpness when I submitted it. Something I knew I would get marked down on!<br/> <br/>Thanks for the kind comments! James.</td>', 'Thank you snaffles. You have given me plenty of food for thought. I really like IreneMs work and sure would like to try a similar shot some time. I need a remote flash! As for this shot I am happy with the score. I realised it lacked sharpness when I submitted it. Something I knew I would get marked down on! Thanks for the kind comments! James.', '2009-04-28 04:13:22.000000', NULL, 0),
